@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-06-09

Feature: Share URL Command
  "CLI handler for mason url: print the short or long public URL for one share ref."

  Provides:
    - cli.newURLCommand @source("symbol:newURLCommand")
    - cli.shareURL @source("symbol:shareURL")

  Consumes:
    - cli.defaultReadRun
    - cli.resolveShareRef
    - domain.ObjectURL
    - domain.SlugURL

  Invariants:
    - Default output MUST be the served short slug URL including extension
    - --long MUST require an object-path endpoint on the share
    - Missing slug or path endpoints MUST surface as usage_error

  Scenario (happy-path): Short URL default
    Given a share with a slug endpoint
    When mason url s/f76 runs
    Then stdout prints the served short URL

  Scenario (happy-path): Long URL flag
    Given a share with an object-path endpoint
    When mason url --long super/rad/foo.mp3 runs
    Then stdout prints the object-path URL

  Scenario (negative): Long URL without path endpoint
    Given a slug-only share
    When mason url --long runs
    Then a usage_error is returned
